// What KIND of thing a provider is, published beside every provider cell's
// availability (increment E1-1b sec 0.1).
//
// Three of this build's facts are properties of a LAB and are NOT properties of
// a ROUTER: the token-accounting sign (NN48 -- a router's cache inclusivity is
// whatever the upstream it chose reports), the price (a router's price is its
// own, plus its fee, not the lab's), and the observability attribution (apps
// point the OpenAI SDK at the router, so the emitted provider name is the
// lab's). A client that cannot tell the two kinds apart cannot know which of
// its numbers carry those caveats.
//
// UNSPECIFIED is a real answer: it means this build did not declare a kind,
// which is what an older build's response decodes to. It never means LAB.
type ProviderKindV1 int32

const (
	ProviderKindV1_PROVIDER_KIND_V1_UNSPECIFIED ProviderKindV1 = 0
	// Serves its own models from its own inference.
	ProviderKindV1_PROVIDER_KIND_V1_LAB ProviderKindV1 = 1
	// Chooses an upstream per call. The upstream is part of the unit of
	// measurement (NN47) and is not pinned by the model id alone.
	ProviderKindV1_PROVIDER_KIND_V1_ROUTER ProviderKindV1 = 2
)

