// E1-1b: the three OpenRouter slugs this build can address, fetched from
// GET https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/models on 2026-08-19 (415 models) rather
// than remembered.
//
// Each value names a slug in the router's OWN namespace, prefix included, and
// each has a lab-side twin already in the enums above -- which is what makes
// the differentiator "the same model via the lab vs via the router" authorable
// as two candidates over one frozen configuration. `anthropic/claude-sonnet-4.6`
// and `claude-sonnet-4-6` are two different ADDRESSES for one model and this
// build must not be able to confuse them.
//
// All three are aliases rather than dated snapshots -- OpenRouter's slug space
// for these families carries no date suffix -- so a router candidate is doubly
// unpinned: the alias may move and the upstream may change (H-OR-1, E1-4's to
// close). Visible in the identifier, which is what NN51 asks for.
